  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "5.9.0\n\nFirst stable release of the Customization API package.\n\nThe package covers the whole Customization API: Import, GetProject, DeleteProject, PublishBegin, PublishEnd, GetPublished and UnpublishAll, each with an async version, plus WaitPublishingCompletion to wait until publishing is finished. Publishing supports the current tenant, all tenants or a list of tenants (TenantMode and tenantLoginNames). Failed calls throw ApiException with the server's explanation, and a failed publishing throws CustomizationPublishException with the log.\n\nCHANGES SINCE THE 5.6.0-beta VERSION:\n- The extension class is now CustomizationApiExtensions (it had the same name as its namespace).\n- CustomizationPublishEnd and CustomizationPublishEndAsync are renamed to PublishEnd and PublishEndAsync.\n- CustomizationPublishEnd.isFailed is renamed to IsFailed.\n- Import and PublishBegin now return CustomizationResult, which holds the log of the operation (Log, HasErrors). They used to return a single log record, which did not match the server response and came back empty.\n- PublishBegin and PublishBeginAsync take IEnumerable of project names instead of List.\n- PublishEnd sends a request body. Without it, current servers answered 415 Unsupported Media Type, which also broke WaitPublishingCompletion.\n- WaitPublishingCompletion reports a failed publishing even if the server also marks it as completed, and has a timeout. WaitPublishingCompletionAsync supports cancellation.\n- Some failures, such as a project that is not found, are answered by the server with a successful status and an error record in the log. Check CustomizationResult.HasErrors.\n- XML documentation for the whole API.",
